{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a cobbler-scaffold \"stitch\" task (ID 5547) to implement `cmd/chmod/main.go` for the go-unix-utils project. The task scope is limited to **core mode parsing and application** covering srd089 requirements R1.1 (octal mode), R1.2 (symbolic mode), R1.3 (multiple file operands), and R1.4 (error handling/exit codes). The task description also mentions \"--help and --version output\" as R4, though this doesn't directly correspond to the SRD's R1.4. Only one file needs to be created: `cmd/chmod/main.go`. No test file is in scope. The task explicitly forbids git commands, filesystem exploration, and scope creep beyond the specified requirements.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU chmod utility verified via differential testing against `gchmod`\n   - Octal mode parsing (e.g., 755, 0644) for absolute permission setting\n   - Symbolic mode parsing: `[ugoa][+-=][rwxXst]` with comma-separated clauses (e.g., `u+x,go=rx`)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - required for all cmd/ utilities\n   - `os.Chmod` for applying computed modes to files\n   - Function size limit of 40 lines (hard limit from execution constitution E8)\n   - File size limit of 500 lines (E9)\n   - Copyright header required: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - No git commands allowed - managed externally by orchestrator\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd089-chmod.yaml` (READ)\n     - This is the SRD defining all chmod requirements\n     - R1: Mode specification - R1.1 octal, R1.2 symbolic with comma-separated clauses, R1.3 multiple files, R1.4 exit 1 on access errors\n     - R2: Recursive (-R), verbose (-v), changes (-c), silent (-f) — NOT in scope for this task\n     - R3: Special bits (setuid/setgid/sticky), --reference — NOT in scope for this task\n     - R4: Exit codes (0 success, 1 failure) and SIGPIPE handling\n     - Non-goals: No SELinux, no --preserve-root\n     - Package contract imports: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n   \n   - `cmd/chmod/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - The sole deliverable file for this task\n     - Must implement: argument parsing, octal mode support, symbolic mode support, multi-file processing, error handling, SIGPIPE\n   \n   - Key existing pkg/ patterns (from inline source):\n     - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`: `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - must call at start of main\n     - `pkg/sys/fileinfo.go`: `Stat()`, `Lstat()`, `FileInfo` struct with Mode field\n     - All cmd/ utilities follow pattern: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` first, then flag parsing, then execution\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - only one tool call was made (Read of SRD file) which succeeded.\n   - Notable discrepancy: The task description says requirement R4 is \"--help and --version output\" but the SRD's R1.4 is about exit code 1 on file access errors. Need to implement both interpretations.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD successfully to understand full requirement scope\n   - Identified that only R1.x requirements are in scope (not R2, R3 recursive/verbose/reference features)\n   - Was about to begin implementation planning when summary was requested\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive task specification including role, repository_files, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source_code, requirement_states), context, execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description, shared_protocols, package_contracts, and constraints. This is the cobbler stitch task prompt.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT