{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NrKRekFTSXE9G7GJ9rgP52","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me compile the findings into a comprehensive report.\n\n## Patterns in go-unix-utils cmd/ Implementations\n\nBased on my analysis of the codebase, here are the key patterns used in existing cmd/ implementations:\n\n### 1. **Copyright Headers**\nAll files follow the same pattern:\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n```\n\n### 2. **Help and Version Text**\nDefined as module-level constants:\n```go\nconst helpText = `Usage: <cmd> [OPTION]...\n<description>\n\n  -<short>, --<long>   description\n      --help     display this help and exit\n      --version  output version information and exit\n`\n\nconst versionText = `<cmd> (go-unix-utils) dev\n`\n```\n\n### 3. **Main Function Structure**\nEvery main() follows this pattern:\n1. Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` immediately (to handle broken pipes gracefully)\n2. Parse arguments\n3. Handle the main logic\n4. Handle errors with proper error messages to stderr\n5. Call `os.Exit()` with appropriate exit codes\n\nExit codes used:\n- `os.Exit(0)` for success or when handling SIGPIPE\n- `os.Exit(1)` for general errors or stderr write failures\n- `os.Exit(2)` for argument parsing errors (seen in `sort`)\n\n### 4. **Argument Parsing Approach**\n**Manual parsing** (no flag package used). Pattern:\n- Iterate through `os.Args[1:]`\n- Handle `--help` and `--version` first (exit with 0 immediately)\n- Handle `--` (end of options marker)\n- Distinguish between long flags `--flag` and short flags `-f`\n- For long flags with values: support both `--flag=value` and `--flag value` forms\n- For short flags with values: support both `-fabcdef value` and `-fvalue` forms\n- Collect positional arguments separately\n\n### 5. **SIGPIPE Handler**\nFrom `/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`:\n```go\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n    c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n    signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n    go func() {\n        <-c\n        os.Exit(0)\n    }()\n}\n```\n- Creates a buffered signal channel\n- Spawns a goroutine that exits cleanly when SIGPIPE arrives\n- Safe to call multiple times (each call starts its own goroutine)\n\n### 6. **Error Handling Pattern**\nConsistent error reporting to stderr:\n```go\nif err != nil {\n    fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"<cmd>: %s\\n\", err)\n    fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try '<cmd> --help' for more information.\")\n    os.Exit(<code>)\n}\n```\n\n### Concrete Examples\n\n**Simple Example (pwd)**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5547/cmd/pwd/main.go`\n- Manual short and long flag parsing\n- Two modes (logical/physical)\n- Validates that no operands are provided\n\n**Medium Complexity (cat)**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5547/cmd/cat/main.go`\n- Global boolean flag variables\n- Complex flag handling with combined short flags\n- Sophisticated line transformation logic\n- Handles SIGPIPE specially (exits 0 immediately)\n\n**Complex Example (split)**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5547/cmd/split/main.go`\n- Struct-based options (more maintainable for many flags)\n- Long flags with value parsing helpers (`longOptValue`)\n- Short flags with value extraction\n- Positional arguments assignment function\n- Multiple parsing modes (lines, bytes, line-bytes, chunks)\n- Comprehensive error handling\n\n**Another Pattern (sort)**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5547/cmd/sort/main.go`\n- Separates flag parsing into `parseLongPrefix` (for flags with = syntax) and `parseLongFlag` (for regular long flags)\n- Dedicated helper functions for specific complex arguments\n- Enum types for mode/check variants\n- Exit code 2 for usage errors (matching GNU coreutils convention)"}]}